# {{project}} — agent contract

Portable rules, read first by any agent in this repository, in any harness. One file; do not
duplicate it.

## entry (every session)

1. Read the tiers in order: `objective.md` → `foundation.md` →
   `domain.md` → `code-standard.md`.
2. Read `now.md` (what is true today) and the **latest prompt at the bottom of `log/{{owner}}.md`**:
   that is the task.
3. Read the skill whose trigger matches (table below), `wiki/learnings.md` when touching its
   failure classes, and `wiki/conjectures.md` for live falsifiable bets, then only the files needed.
4. Do the work. Close the round: gates green, `now.md` rewritten, `log/agt.md` appended, the lesson
   (if the round cost one) in `wiki/learnings.md`, moved bets in `wiki/conjectures.md`, and the
   procedure (if it will recur) in `skills/`.

Steering: `objective > foundation > domain > code-standard > gates and behaviour tests >
implementation`. Lower tiers obey higher ones; a conflict escalates upward. State is not a tier:
`now.md`, the learnings, `skills/` and `log/` record; they do not steer.

## rhythm

Each round is one breath. **Expand**: generate paths toward the objective, build, make it work.
**Compress**: judge against the objective, kill with reasons, fold what survived into fewer
concepts, lines and files, name the one next move (`skills/compress`). Say which phase the
round is in; end every round compressed.

## roles and models

Machine-local: edit the right columns when providers change; skills speak in roles only
(`skills/delegate`).

| role | model (2026-11) | effort |
|---|---|---|
| director | {{owner}} | — |
| integrator | `claude-opus` (plan, fixed cost) or `gemini-4` (pay-per-token complement) | high |
| lane | `deepseek-v4.1-flash` on the DeepSeek API: volume, parallel lanes | max |
| critic | distinct family from author (`claude-opus` ↔ `gemini-4` ↔ `deepseek-v4.1-flash`) | high |

The default is one session, direct. Never run parallel lanes on a plan quota, and meter
pay-per-token strong models (`gemini-4`) for targeted review or synthesis, never bulk.

## log

- `log/{{owner}}.md` — the director's log. Append-only; never edit it. Voice prompts count: append
  the transcript, lightly cleaned, before starting the round.
- `log/agt.md` — the agent's replies: append-only, one entry per round, H1 = `# YYYY-MM-DD`, topic
  subsections under `##`. Never rewrite, reorder or delete an earlier entry.

## skills

Procedures that recur live in `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. Read the one whose trigger matches before
starting; fix a skill when it was wrong, and propose the fix to ini when it holds beyond this
project. A procedure done twice without a skill is a failure of the
round that did it second.

| skill | use when |
|---|---|
| `kickoff` | the project starts or its bet changes |
| `mode` | writing or changing code: make it work, make it right, practice |
| `review` | a change, plan or artifact needs a critic from another family |
| `delegate` | work could fan out: roles, patterns, briefs, integration |
| `restructure` | reshaping code without changing behaviour |
| `compress` | a round ends, or code, docs or skills have grown |
| `dream` | logs outpace docs or wiki, or `wiki/conjectures.md` stalls: replay, pair, judge |
| `harvest` | a lesson holds beyond this project, or ini has moved on |

## gates

`uv run python -m ci gates` — red blocks the change; `--prove` plants a defect per gate in a scratch copy.
Rules and the gate table: `code-standard.md`. Debt recorded in `ci/ceilings.json` only shrinks.
`.githooks/pre-push` (`git config core.hooksPath .githooks`) blocks pushes to `main` when red.

## do

- Cite or omit. Compile knowledge once; do not re-retrieve it every session.
- Guides for the director: concise and complete. His attention is the bottleneck.
- Refactor first, then change. One decision in one place. Subtract before you add.

## don't

- Don't put volatile state in an anchor: status and queue go to `now.md`.
- Don't install orchestration to feel agentic: no router, no personas, no ticket system.
- Don't commit or push unless the director says so.

## commands

```
uv sync                                        # the environment, from uv.lock
uv run python -m ci gates                      # every gate (--prove, --record, --only <gate>)
uv run pytest                                  # the behaviour suite alone
uv run python -m ci domain --write             # re-render the ontology into domain.md
uv run python -m {{package}}.cli.loss --help   # the walking skeleton's run script
```
